Z||000000||fogglethorpe||08-21-2001||07:06 AM||||Some stories start, "Once upon a time..."<BR>Some stories have rhythm, some stories have rhyme<BR>Some stories are of good things, some are of bad<BR>Some have happy endings, some endings are sad<BR>But this story is not like any of those...<BR>This story is nonsense and anything goes<P>There once lived a pig who ate sauerkraut<BR>'Til his outside was in, his inside was out<BR>The sauerkraut gave him an allergy<BR>His eyes got so watery he couldn't see<BR>He sneezed and he wheezed again and again<BR>'Til his outside came out, his inside went in<BR>And he said, "I'll have no more of this stuff about;<BR>sauerkraut turns my snout inside out, no doubt!"<P>There once were two feet that belonged to a man<BR>Each one always wished that it was a hand<BR>They wouldn't walk or kick a ball<BR>They wanted to wave to friends or draw<BR>They didn't want to wear socks or shoes<BR>They much preferred gloves, if they could choose<BR>The man was unhappy, and unsure what to do<BR>Then proclaimed an idea that was totally new<BR>"With my legs toward the sky and my head near the street<BR>Maybe my hands can be my feet!"<BR>The problem was solved, a solution was found-<BR>He decided to live his life upside down<BR>The only detail he didn't plan<BR>Was shopping for shoes to fit his hands<P>Some stories are thought, some stories are said<BR>Some stories are read while you are in bed<BR>Some stories are written or sang like a song<BR>Some are quite short and some go too long<BR>But this one is neither, no this one's just right<BR>Because it is ending now- Good night!<P><BR>...........<BR>Just when I closed the door on reality, it came in through the window...||||reg||1
